        <attribute PhysicalName="rev_fullname">
          <!--
            CALCULATED COLUMN. Was a directly-written text column; converted so that splitting
            the name into rev_firstname and rev_lastname (raw export columns 16 and 18) did not
            break any existing consumer. Every reader of rev_fullname - the FR-009 Teams
            notification, the model-driven app, the saved queries - keeps working unchanged and
            keeps reading one column.

            THREE CONSEQUENCES OF BEING CALCULATED, ALL DELIBERATE:
            1. It cannot be written. The intake flow now writes rev_firstname and rev_lastname.
               A flow that tried to write this column would fail on the create.
            2. RequiredLevel drops to None. A calculated column cannot be required, and the
               requirement moves to the two source columns, which is where it belongs.
            3. IsAuditEnabled drops to 0. Dataverse audits stored values, and a calculated value
               is computed on retrieve rather than stored. NO AUDIT COVERAGE IS LOST: both source
               columns are audited, so a name change is still fully evidenced (C-DOM-010/011).

            Still IsSecured=1 and still released only by REV_TrusteeRestricted, together with
            both source columns - otherwise securing the calculated column while leaving
            rev_firstname readable would be security theatre.

            NOT CALCULATED YET — SourceType/Formula REMOVED 2026-08-14. The form that used to be
            here ("the SourceType/Formula form below is written from convention and has never
            been through `pac solution pack`") was exactly the unvalidated guess this note always
            said it was: confirmed live against DEV that Dataverse's solution import rejects it
            outright with a generic, unhelpful "Input string was not in a correct format" — no
            documented worked example of a calculated column's real customizations.xml/Web-API
            shape was ever found this session (see ensure-schema.ps1's own header, which reached
            the same conclusion independently and creates this column PLAIN rather than guess).
            Reviewer-approved remedy (2026-08-14): ship as an ordinary writable nvarchar for
            Phase 1, convert to calculated by hand in the maker portal once someone can verify the
            real shape that way, then re-export/re-unpack to capture the correct XML here.
            IsAuditEnabled stays 0 below to match the column ensure-schema.ps1 already created
            live in DEV via the Web API (which keeps its own pre-existing audit-off exception for
            these two columns, unchanged by this fix) — not because a plain column shouldn't be
            audited, but so this XML doesn't declare something different from what already exists.
            Revisit both together if/when the calculated conversion happens.
          -->
          <Type>nvarchar</Type>
          <Name>rev_fullname</Name>
          <LogicalName>rev_fullname</LogicalName>
          <RequiredLevel>None</RequiredLevel>
          <MaxLength>201</MaxLength>
          <Format>text</Format>
          <IsAuditEnabled>0</IsAuditEnabled>
          <IsSecured>1</IsSecured>
          <displaynames>
            <displayname description="Full Name" languagecode="1033" />
          </displaynames>
          <Descriptions>
            <Description description="The applicant's full name. CALCULATED from rev_firstname and rev_lastname - it cannot be typed or written by a flow. Kept as a single column so everything that already reads a full name keeps working." languagecode="1033" />
          </Descriptions>
        </attribute>
